---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "30 August 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms — PaceStreak"
  description="Terms of use for the PaceStreak website while the product is in development."
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="wrap max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] text-dim">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose-page mt-10">
        <p>
          These terms cover <strong>this website</strong>. There is no product
          to sign up for yet, no account, and no payment — so there is not much
          to agree to.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site is</h2>
        <p>
          An informational site about PaceStreak, a workout streak tracker that
          is still being built. Everything described here is a statement of
          intent about unreleased software, not a promise of a feature on a
          date.
        </p>

        <h2>Early access</h2>
        <p>
          Emailing <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a
          > puts you on a list. It does not create an account, guarantee access,
          or commit either side to anything. Invitations go out in batches and
          may take a while.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          This site is provided as is. We try to keep it accurate and available
          — availability is published at{" "}
          <a href="https://status.pacestreak.com">status.pacestreak.com</a> — but
          nothing here is guaranteed to be correct, current, or uninterrupted.
        </p>

        <h2>Content and code</h2>
        <p>
          The PaceStreak name, logo and wordmark are ours. The source code of
          this site is published under{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/PaceStreak">AGPL-3.0</a>: you may read,
          modify and redistribute it under that licence, which requires you to
          offer your source to anyone you run a modified version for over a
          network. The licence covers the code, not the brand.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          Do not attempt to disrupt the site or the infrastructure behind it. If
          you find a security issue, please report it privately to{" "}
          <a href="mailto:hello@pacestreak.com">hello@pacestreak.com</a> rather
          than disclosing it publicly — see the{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/PaceStreak/.github/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
            >security policy</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          When the product launches, these terms will be replaced by ones that
          actually describe a service with accounts and data. Until then this
          page is versioned publicly, so every change has a commit and a date.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
